# Orbit YouTube — cutscene / picture rules

## Hard assembly rules

1. **Never reuse a cutscene** in a single video. Each B-roll / card / plate filename appears at most once.
2. **Never loop cutscenes.** Play once at native duration. No `stream_loop`, ping-pong, or freeze-extend — including Seedance / Veo / animated beds.
3. **Never slow-mo stretch** (`setpts` > 1×) to fill VO. Slow-mo makes the episode feel laggy.
4. **Never use long still-pan fills as the main picture.** Still boards are a **short bridge only** (target ≤ ~4s leftover after motion). If VO needs more picture, **generate more unique motion clips** — do not pad with minutes of Ken Burns / hero stills.
5. **Exception:** Orbit character PiP may loop (character bed only).
6. Prefer vibrant, distinct scenery (planets, surfaces, telescopes, atmospheres). Avoid empty distant-galaxy / static starfield plates.
7. Include Orbit **brand intro** (~1s) and **like/subscribe outro** plus matching VO CTA.
8. **Never animate text plates** with zoompan/Ken Burns. Title cards and brand stings must be locked stills.

## Motion coverage (plan before generate)

Before locking an episode edit, size the clip inventory so **usable 1× motion covers most of VO picture time**:

- Gemini Veo clips are typically **~8s** and often **degrade in the last ~2s**. Plan on **~5.5–6s usable** per clip after a soft tail trim.
- **Budget:** `usable_clips × ~6s  ≥  0.75 × VO_picture_seconds` (aim higher for hero sections).
- Example: ~10–12 min VO picture ≈ need **~75–100+ unique 8s clips** (scale up for longer VO).
- If coverage is short: add **new unique variants** (extra prompts / p1/p2/p3 takes) — never stretch, loop, or long-still the gap.

## AI Studio Veo UI guards (default CG path — Ultra)

1. Use **`04_Audio/tools/orbit_aistudio_veo_ui.py`** (Playwright → AI Studio with Ultra). **Not** ElevenLabs Image & Video. **Not** API key as default (`orbit_gemini_veo.py` = fallback only).
2. **Start / prompt image = Orbit only.** Abort if non-Orbit refs bind. Forbid **Eiffel Tower / Paris / architectural blueprints / parchment schematics**.
3. Prompt lock: no readable text / logos / UI; **SILENT PICTURE ONLY**; British VO mixed in edit from ElevenLabs.
4. Strip audio on download. Spot-check first ~1s and last ~2s; quarantine rejects.
5. In edit: optional soft **tail trim (~2–2.5s)** when inventory already covers VO without long stills.

## Legacy

ElevenLabs Omni / in-app Veo Playwright scripts (`_generate_omni_*.py`) are legacy. Do not use for new episodes.

## Lessons (JWST v004 — 2026-08)

- Slow-mo stretch fixed “lag” but was wrong; **1× motion** is correct.
- Root cause of static feel: **too few unique clips for VO length**.
- Fix path: **regenerate more unique motion plates** via AI Studio Veo (Ultra), rebuild master + Shorts, keep ElevenLabs VO/music.

